      "id": "e1",
      "title": "Nationalities: man and woman",
      "body": "A nationality is an adjective. It matches the person: add -e for a woman (français → française). Many end in -ien for a man and -ienne for a woman (canadien → canadienne). In speech, the feminine says the final consonant. In writing, you add the letters. The full rule comes in Unit 4."
